papers per year if U.S.

513
00:28:11,004 --> 00:28:14,304
governance merely matched the average rich country.

514
00:28:14,344 --> 00:28:15,364
You don't need a revolution.

515
00:28:16,384 --> 00:28:17,564
You need a reallocation.

516
00:28:18,544 --> 00:28:20,604
Revolutions require guns.

517
00:28:20,664 --> 00:28:22,704
Reallocations require spreadsheets.

518
00:28:23,524 --> 00:28:26,294
You are surprisingly bad at both.

519
00:28:26,464 --> 00:28:28,044
But nobody fights to recover it.

520
00:28:28,584 --> 00:28:30,244
Same pattern as this entire chapter:

521
00:28:31,084 --> 00:28:34,984
each corporation gains one hundred million dollars (worth hiring a thousand

522
00:28:34,984 --> 00:28:35,644
lobbyists).

523
00:28:36,304 --> 00:28:39,244
Each citizen loses thousands (not worth a phone call).

524
00:28:40,064 --> 00:28:42,504
The losses are too spread out to organize around.

525
00:28:43,084 --> 00:28:45,304
The gains are too concentrated to give up.

526
00:28:46,284 --> 00:28:49,704
But what if curing disease was more profitable than treating it?

527
00:28:50,364 --> 00:28:52,084
What if peace paid better than war?

528
00:28:52,764 --> 00:28:56,044
What if you could point the same corruption machine at something useful?

529
00:28:56,964 --> 00:28:59,024
That's what a one percent treaty does.

530
00:28:59,404 --> 00:29:00,884
It redirects the papers.

531
00:29:01,284 --> 00:29:05,624
But redirecting papers into a system run by the same committees and lobbyists

532
00:29:05,984 --> 00:29:09,064
just creates a new pile for the same parasites to feed on.

533
00:29:09,844 --> 00:29:11,454
You need two more things.

534
00:29:11,964 --> 00:29:15,824
Incentive Alignment Bonds turn the bribery machine against itself.

535
00:29:16,944 --> 00:29:21,324
Politicians who vote for the treaty get reelection papers and cushy post-office

536
00:29:21,324 --> 00:29:21,884
careers.

537
00:29:22,364 --> 00:29:26,384
Politicians who vote against it watch that same money go to their opponents.

538
00:29:26,964 --> 00:29:28,314
You don't fight the corruption.

539
00:29:28,824 --> 00:29:30,084
You outbid it.

540
00:29:30,184 --> 00:29:30,824
Same machine.

541
00:29:31,184 --> 00:29:31,844
Same greed.

542
00:29:32,344 --> 00:29:33,104
Different output.

543
00:29:34,044 --> 00:29:37,584
Wishocracy replaces the committees that lobbyists capture.

544
00:29:38,324 --> 00:29:42,164
Instead of five hundred and thirty-five congressmen deciding which diseases

545
00:29:42,164 --> 00:29:44,744
get funded (based on who bought them dinner),

546
00:29:45,384 --> 00:29:49,944
eight billion people make pairwise comparisons, and an algorithm allocates

547
00:29:49,944 --> 00:29:50,904
the budget.

548
00:29:51,004 --> 00:29:52,044
No committee chairs.

549
00:29:52,164 --> 00:29:53,304
No fundraising quotas.

550
00:29:53,724 --> 00:29:58,384
No lobbyist can bribe eight billion random voters, and the only way to try

551
00:29:58,384 --> 00:30:02,484
is to offer them something they actually want (which is the system working

552
00:30:02,484 --> 00:30:03,404
correctly, for once).

553
00:30:04,264 --> 00:30:08,044
The plan is to give the bribers more money than the other bribers are giving

554
00:30:08,044 --> 00:30:11,444
them, and then replace the thing they were bribing with an equation.

555
00:30:12,104 --> 00:30:13,884
On Wishonia, this took twelve minutes.

556
00:30:14,404 --> 00:30:18,484
On Earth, it will probably take longer, because you will want to argue about

557
00:30:18,484 --> 00:30:19,004
it first.

558
00:30:31,452 --> 00:30:36,992
Thank you so much for taking the time to end war and disease, but if at

559
00:30:36,992 --> 00:30:41,212
any point you decide you're too busy, please press the share button on your

560
00:30:41,212 --> 00:30:44,912
glowing rectangle in case one of your friends have a free afternoon to end

561
00:30:44,912 --> 00:30:45,952
war and disease instead.

562
00:30:46,572 --> 00:30:50,912
And if you're too busy to even do that, please leave a really, really, really

563
00:30:50,912 --> 00:30:55,072
good rating and review so we overcome the pro -war algorithmic suppression

564
00:30:55,072 --> 00:30:58,632
and find someone with more spare time for ending wars and diseases.

565
00:30:59,192 --> 00:31:01,392
The good review doesn't have to be true, they don't check.

566
00:31:01,932 --> 00:31:05,992
But if you're too busy to even do that, the absolute least you could do

567
00:31:05,992 --> 00:31:11,612
is take 15 seconds to go to WarOnDisease.org and make your wishocratic allocation,

568
00:31:12,032 --> 00:31:15,592
telling us what fraction of humanity's resources should go to explosions

569
00:31:15,592 --> 00:31:17,052
versus clinical trials.

570
00:31:17,332 --> 00:31:17,832
And vote!

571
00:31:18,252 --> 00:31:22,512
If the 1% treaty passes, your vote will be personally to blame for saving

572
00:31:22,512 --> 00:31:27,132
2.6 lives and preventing 468,000 hours of suffering.

573
00:31:27,132 --> 00:31:29,832
Go to WarOnDisease.org right now.

574
00:31:30,232 --> 00:31:30,792
Love you, bye!
